  "meta": {
    "probe": "ur-stencil-b",
    "reAuthorOf": "examples/probes/ur-stencil-b.json",
    "target": "same lineage as ur-stencil, different object: a square record label rather than a poster -- centre hole, catalogue text, matrix numbers, one red mark",
    "method": "the same label as the v0 probe. Every one of the four clip rects that removed nothing is gone: each disc is now a circle clip and the thing painted inside it is a plain rect, so the round shape is the clip rather than a region that happened to be routed through the polygon path by a rectangle wrapped around it. The catalogue and matrix type moves to real faces -- Anton for the side letter, Barlow Condensed for the title, Share Tech Mono and Space Mono for the matrix and runout, which is what a stamped runout actually is. print carries misregister and grain.",
    "notDone": "text still cannot be set on a curve. text.rotate turns a whole line about its anchor, which is a chord, not an arc, and there is no per-character placement, so the ring of catalogue type that defines this object is still two straight lines above and below the spindle. The ring layout still has no sweep, so the red spokes are still spread around the whole circle."
  },
